# Always push to git

When finishing a task that changed files in this repo:

1. Create a git commit for the relevant changes (unless the user said not to commit).
2. Push the commit to the remote immediately after a successful commit (`git push`).
3. Do not wait for a separate push request.

If push fails (auth, network, protected branch), report the error and the commit that is ready to push.
